    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of September 22, 2023\n\nThis Act can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n[Certified on 19th of September, 2023]\n\nCHARTERED INSTITUTE OF TRANSPORT OF SRI LANKA(INCORPORATION) (AMENDMENT)ACT, No. 18 OF 2023\n\nChartered Institute of Transport of Sri Lanka (Incorporation) (Amendment)Act, No. 18 of 2023\n\n1\n\n[Certified on 19th of September, 2023]\n\nL.D.\u2014O. (Inc.) 4/2019\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE CHARTERED INSTITUTE OF TRANSPORT OFSRI LANKA (INCORPORATION) ACT, NO. 8 OF 2000\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Chartered Institute ofTransport of Sri Lanka (Incorporation) (Amendment) Act,No. 18 of 2023.\n\n2.The long title to the Chartered Institute of Transportof Sri Lanka (Incorporation) Act, No. 8 of 2000, (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amendedby the substitution, for the words \u201cChartered Institute ofTransport of Sri Lanka.\u201d of the words \u201cChartered Institute ofLogistics and Transport of Sri Lanka.\u201d.\n\n3.(1) In the principal enactment and in any other writtenlaw there shall be substituted for the words \u201cCharteredInstitute of Transport of Sri Lanka\u201d wherever such wordsappear in the principal enactment and such other written lawof the words \u201cChartered Institute of Logistics and Transportof Sri Lanka\u201d.\n\n(2) Every reference to the \u201cChartered Institute of Transportof Sri Lanka\u201d in any notice, notification, contract,communication or other document shall be read andconstrued as a reference to the \u201cChartered Institute of Logisticsand Transport of Sri Lanka\u201d."
