    "chunk_text": "Destruction. of evidence of proceeds of crime to bean offence.\n\n11Proceeds of Crime Act, No. 5 of 2025\n\n10. Any person served with a notice under section 68 of this Act who-\n\n(a) refuses to accept;\n\n(b) fails to respond truthfully to; or\n\nresponse or wilfully makes a misrepresentation or act of deception to,\n\nsuch notice commits an offence.\n\n11. Any person who intentionally aids, advices, induces, influences, or threatens another to whom a notice under section 68 has been served to provide a false or misleading or deceptive response to such notice, commits an offence.\n\n12. Any person who presents a false or misleading claim, description or representation to the High Court for the purpose of preventing the judicial freezing of any property, discharge of any property, or having a judicial freezing order varied or vacated, commits an offence.\n\n13. Any person who presents a false or misleading claim, description, representation or an affidavit containing a false or misleading description or a false document to the High Court for the purpose of preventing the forfeiture of or the release of any property, commits an offence.\n\n14. (1) Any person, who attempts or conspires to commit any offence under section 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, or 13, or aids or abets the commission of such offence commits an offence.\n\n(2) In this section \u201cabet\u201d, \u201caid\u201d and \u201cconspiracy\u201d shall have the same meaning as in sections 100, 111 and 113 of the Penal Code.\n\nFailure to accept a notice or provision of false response to a notice to bean offence.\n\nAiding the provision of false response to a notice to be an offence.\n\nPresenting a false or misleading claim to prevent judicial freezing to bean offence.\n\nPresenting a false or misleading claim to prevent forfeiture to be an offence.\n\nAiding and abetting an offence under section 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, or 13 to be an offence.\n\nProceeds of Crime Act, No. 5 of 202512"
