    "chunk_text": "aligned civil society organizations of which the mandate shall include the development of transparency, strengthening of anti-corruption measures or advancement of objectives of criminal justice in consultation with the Minister assigned the subject of Social Services.\n\n133Proceeds of Crime Act, No. 5 of 2025\n\n99. (1) The Minister shall appoint from amongst the appointed members the person who in his opinion is the most suitable person to perform the functions of the Chairman of the Board and thereafter record the reasons for such appointment.\n\n(2) The Chairman shall be the head of the Authority and shall preside over meetings of the Board.\n\n(3) The Chairman may resign from his office by letter addressed to the Minister and such resignation shall be effective from the date on which it is accepted by the Minister.\n\n(4) The Minister may for reasons assigned remove the Chairman from the office of Chairman and report such removal with reasons therefor to Parliament by making an address to Parliament.\n\n(5) Where the Chairman is temporarily unable to perform the duties of his office due to ill health, other infirmity, prolonged absence from Sri Lanka or any other cause, the Minister may appoint any other appointed member to act as Chairman in addition to his normal duties as an appointed member.\n\n100. (1) Every appointed member of the Board shall \u2013\n\n(a) be not more than seventy years of age as at the\n\ndate of appointment to the Board;\n\n(b) be of sound mind; and\n\n(c) be a competent person with integrity and good\n\nrepute.\n\nChairman of the Board\n\nDisqualifications from being a member of the Board\n\n134Proceeds of Crime Act, No. 5 of 2025\n\n(2) A person shall be disqualified from being appointed or continuing as a member of the Board, if such person \u2013\n\n(a) is or becomes a member of Parliament or of any\n\nProvincial Council or any local authority;\n\n(b) is not or ceases to be a citizen of Sri Lanka;\n\n(c) is a person who having been declared insolvent\n\nor bankrupt under any law in Sri Lanka;"
